---NOTES---
This canonical OCR file is Part 12 of `மாஜி கடவுள்கள் / Former Gods`. It begins by continuing the Egyptian afterlife discussion from Part 11 and ends mid-sentence after Miach’s death. No canonical `maji_kadavulgal13.md` exists; the archived `maji_kadavulgal14.md` begins with the grammatical continuation, “At the place where they buried him, 365 plants sprouted.” The English ending therefore preserves the handoff and does not invent a missing Part 13. Celtic names are normalized in English where identification is clear: Danu, Bile, Dagda, Boann, Brigid, Aengus, Midir, Ogma, Bodb, Morrigu, Nuada, Elatha, Bres, Dian Cecht, and Miach. The Tamil OCR source remains verbatim, including damaged names and scan artifacts. Historical mythological and comparative claims are translated as the source’s argument without independent endorsement.
